From 84f571c563d07dd3d82af83f75b465ee35f9a5b6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sfxnz <sfxnz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:30:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] inkling2: batch multi-stream conv/attn, bucket global
 last_pos, slot-agnostic graphs

Commit 2 (Lever 1, 100% lossless, ~1 KB scratch accounted in planScratchMode):
- Batch tf_ink2_conv across all active streams in one launch per site using per-stream
  state_bases and hist_bases device tables (writing local-row hist for exact rewind).
- Batch attention prep_fp8, rel_table, attend, and merge across all active streams in one
  launch per visit (populating seg_of, multi-stream segs with slot-relative element offsets
  for sliding caches and per-slot page tables for 1M paged FP8 global KV, and combined tiles).
- Bucket global last_pos (1K/4K/16K/32K/64K/256K/context) and cap split global grid.z
  slots_rh to active 1024-token sub-chunks instead of hardcoding context - 1 (eliminating
  empty global CTA blocks at short/medium contexts while keeping 1M paged KV intact).
- Replace per-slot Shape.parts graph key with slot-agnostic Shape (adapted from MiaAI-Lab
  commit 9e3cf20b patch 0014-mini-wide-graphs-prompt-rows.patch) and batch conv backups
  through a single tf_ink2_copy_spans launch.
- Update kernels_test.zig for 128-thread rel_table and add short-context split grid.z tests.
